      "description": "US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth dug in for a fight Tuesday against his potential impeachment in Congress, telling reporters that a rogue lawmaker is targeting him over \"policy disagreements\" and not the high crimes or offenses the nation's founders intended.\nThe embattled Pentagon chief spoke at his first press briefing from the five-sided building in six months, launching a counteroffensive against outgoing Representative Thomas Massie's effort to impeach him over his handling of the unpopular war against Iran and other actions.\n\"In the 250 years of our American republic, no Secretary of War or Secretary of Defence has ever been impeached for carrying out lawful military operations,\" Hegseth told reporters.\nThe briefing was Hegseth's first since May even as the US military has kept up intermittent operations against Iran as well as fatal strikes on alleged drug-smuggling boats in Latin America.\nRepresentative Thomas Massie, a Kentucky Republican who lost his primary to a ...",
